 "text": "Paganism is the older Celtic religion. The Church did not erase it at once. Some ancient festivals returned in Christian form. Lughnasa became the climb of Croagh Patrick, also called the Reek. People made this climb on the last Sunday of July. The local name Domhnach Chrom Dubh means Crom Dubh's Sunday. That name keeps a trace of a pagan god Patrick overcame.",
